

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
# Full guide: CONTRIBUTING.md. Enable this template once per clone with:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
# Lines starting with "#" are removed from the message.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# --- Header (required) -------------------------------------------------------
# Aim for 72 characters or fewer (the hard limit is 100). Write the subject in
# the imperative mood and lower case, with no full stop at the end:
#   "add trim handles to takes", not "Added trim handles." or "Adds ...".
#
# Types:
#   feat      a new feature for users
#   fix       a bug fix
#   docs      documentation only
#   refactor  a code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf      a performance improvement
#   test      adding or fixing tests
#   build     build system, packaging (electron-builder) or dependencies
#   ci        GitHub Actions and other CI configuration
#   chore     maintenance that does not touch src/ or the shipped app
#   revert    reverts an earlier commit
#
# Scopes (optional, pick the closest one):
#   generate   the Generate view and the job queue
#   prompt     the prompt editor and @ImageN reference checks
#   library    characters, environments, outfits and the prompt library
#   assets     reference images and asset folders on disk
#   sequences  sequences, clips, takes, trims, preview, storyboards and own clips
#   editor     Redigera: edits, versions, operations, voices and transcripts
#   images     stills and Venice's image models (Skapa bild)
#   export     ffmpeg export of sequences
#   agent      agent connection: approvals, activity, the agent guide
#   mcp        the MCP server, its tools and transport
#   db         SQLite schema and migrations
#   ui         shared UI components, layout and styling
#   settings   the Settings view, the base folder and profiles
#   build      electron-vite, electron-builder and packaging
#   deps       dependency updates
#   docs       README, docs/ and other documentation
#
# --- Body (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Explain what changed and why, not how. Wrap lines at 72 characters.
# Separate the body from the header with one blank line.
#
# --- Footer (optional) -------------------------------------------------------
# Reference issues and flag breaking changes, one per line:
#   Closes #123
#   Refs #45
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks, and how to migrate>
# A breaking change can also be marked with "!" after the type or scope:
#   feat(mcp)!: rename the list_assets tool to list_library
#
# Never put API keys, tokens, real names or personal paths in a commit.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(sequences): continue a clip from the trimmed last frame
#   fix(export): keep audio in sync when a take is trimmed
#   docs(mcp): describe the approval flow for paid generations
#   build(deps): bump electron from 44.5.1 to 44.6.0
